# Review before finishing

Before you report a code change as done, review the diff yourself against these four checks. Fix what fails the check in the same turn.

- **Types.** No new `any`, unchecked casts, or silent widening. Public functions state their inputs and errors in the type system.
- **Errors.** Fallible boundaries use `try/catch` (or the language equivalent). Catch blocks log context and rethrow or return a typed error. Empty catches are not allowed.
- **Modules.** One reason to change per file. Do not grow a function so it fetches, transforms, and renders in the same block; split along that seam.
- **Cost.** Flag work that loops over unbounded input, awaits inside a hot loop, or loads a whole collection to read one field. Prefer a bounded query or a single pass.

```typescript
// Empty catch hides the failure
try {
  await save(row);
} catch {
  return null;
}

// Boundary keeps the cause
try {
  await save(row);
} catch (error) {
  logger.error("save failed", { id: row.id, error });
  throw new SaveError("Unable to save", { cause: error });
}
```
